<div class="content">
  <div class="article">
    <h1>First Aikido Training in Gdynia</h1>

    <p class="lead">
      The biggest barrier before starting is rarely physical - it is practical: <strong>can I come with no experience</strong>,
      <strong>what should I bring</strong>, <strong>what does stepping onto the mat look like</strong> and <strong>will I manage</strong>.
      Below you will find calm, concrete answers.
    </p>

    <p>
      A new season is a good moment for a first class, but you do not have to wait for it to begin.
      At Sesshinkan Dojo intake runs all year round.
    </p>

    <h2>For your first class, bring only what you need</h2>

    <div class="beginner-cards">
      <div class="beginner-card">
        <h3>🥋 Clothing</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>a comfortable sports T-shirt,</li>
          <li>tracksuit bottoms or leggings with no hard elements,</li>
          <li>a clean change of clothes.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="note">You buy a keikogi only once you decide to train regularly.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="beginner-card">
        <h3>💧 Small things</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>a bottle of water,</li>
          <li>a towel,</li>
          <li>a few minutes of spare time before class.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="beginner-card">
        <h3>🧠 Mindset</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>you do not need to know any techniques,</li>
          <li>you do not need to be flexible or "athletic",</li>
          <li>at the start, calm and attention count - not pace.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>What does the first class look like?</h2>

    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step">
        <span class="step-number">1</span>
        <div class="step-content">
          <h4>Entering the dojo</h4>
          <p>You arrive a little early, meet the instructor and get the essential organisational pointers.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="step">
        <span class="step-number">2</span>
        <div class="step-content">
          <h4>Warm-up and basics</h4>
          <p>First come simple movement exercises, the basics of moving, and elements that prepare you for safe work on the mat.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="step">
        <span class="step-number">3</span>
        <div class="step-content">
          <h4>Paired practice</h4>
          <p>Beginners practise with more experienced people or under the instructor's clear guidance. You are not left alone with it.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="step">
        <span class="step-number">4</span>
        <div class="step-content">
          <h4>Check whether it is for you</h4>
          <p>After class you can calmly ask about further training, fees, clothing and training frequency.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>What do beginners fear most?</h2>

    <div class="faq-section">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Do I need to be fit?</h3>
        <p>No. Fitness is built through regularity. The first classes are not an endurance test.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Is Aikido safe to start with?</h3>
        <p>Yes, if you practise in the controlled environment of the dojo and follow the guidance. Techniques are introduced gradually.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Am I too old to start?</h3>
        <p>There is no upper age limit. What matters most is common sense, regularity and adapting training to your capabilities.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>What to do before your first visit?</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>check the <a href="/en/contact.html">dojo schedule and location</a>,</li>
      <li>read the page <a href="/en/aikido-training-gdynia.html">about Aikido training in Gdynia</a>,</li>
      <li>see <a href="/en/biographies/szrajer.html">who teaches and what Sesshinkan Dojo is</a>,</li>
      <li>if you prefer, write or call before your first visit,</li>
      <li>arrive 10-15 minutes early.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Read before you start</h2>

    <p>
      If you want to ease into the subject calmly, also read:
      <a href="/en/blog/who-is-aikido-for.html">who is aikido for</a>,
      <a href="/en/blog/is-aikido-worth-practicing.html">is aikido worth practicing</a>
      and <a href="/en/blog/aikido-at-every-age.html">aikido at every age</a>.
      They complement the practical information before your first step onto the mat well.
    </p>

